<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">AUKUS</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2021">2021</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">AUKUS is a security partnership between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, the United Kingdom and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> announced in September 2021. Its main element provides for Australia to acquire nuclear-powered, conventionally armed submarines, first by purchase from the United States and then of a new shared design. It also covers cooperation in advanced military technologies and reflects concern over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>'s rise in the Indo-Pacific.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aukus.jpg" alt="AUKUS" width="320" height="163" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Canuckguy et al. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AUKUS_signatories_map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
